460 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 423 0 R
/E (Electrical fires are one of the leading causes of property damage and loss of life,often resulting from unnoticed electrical faults.Traditional fire alarm systems are mainly reactive,as they detect smoke or flames only after a fire has already started. This project aims to shift from reactive fire detection to proactive fire prevention by using real-time sensor data and Machine Learning to predict potential fire risks before ignition occurs. An ESP32-based IoT system continuously monitors important electrical and environmental parameters such as temperature,voltage,current,and smoke to identify abnormal conditions.Based on the collected data,the system automatically classifies the level of fire risk and takes preventive actions,including power disconnection,buzzer activation,and SMS alerts,thereby improving electrical safety and enabling early intervention.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
