469 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 424 0 R
/E (Electrical fires are one of the leading causes of property damage and are often detected only after smoke or flames appear.This project proposes an AI-Based Electrical Fire Prevention System that predicts fire hazards before ignition using IoT sensor and Machine Learning.The system continuously monitors temperature, voltage, current, and smoke levels through an ESP32 microcontroller.A machine learning model analyzes the combined sensor data and classifies the fire risk into Safe, Warning, High Risk, and Critical levels.During critical conditions,the system automatically disconnects the power using a relay,activates a buzzer,sends an SMS alert through the SIM800L GSM module,and stores the event for future analysis.This low-cost,real-time solution improves electrical safety in homes,offices,laboratories,and industrial environments by preventing fires before they occur.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
