603 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 429 0 R
/E (The proposed system continuously collects temperature,voltage, current, and smoke readings using sensors connected to an ESP32 microcontroller.The collected sensor data is filtered and preprocessed to remove unwanted variations and prepare it for analysis. The preprocessed data is then given to the proposed Random Forest machine learning classifier,which analyses the sensor parameters and predicts the electrical fire risk.The predicted risk is classified into four levels: Safe,Warning,High Risk, and Critical. When a Critical condition is detected,the system automatically disconnects the power supply through a relay, activates a buzzer,and sends an SMS alert using the SIM800L GSM module.Finally,sensor readings, risk levels, and system actions are stored for monitoring, analysis, and future improvement of the model.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
